Perhaps we can coordinate: those with the best costs for each task type could prioritize those? For example, Shelley has the best triage cost (1.24), so maybe she takes triage? Then we can divide the remaining tasks based on our next best costs. What do you all think?", "blackboard_id": 0}

post_message -- {"blackboard_id": 1, "message": "Gaynell, I'm flexible on taking either docs (3.11) or test (4.36) - both are reasonable options for me. Looking at the public board, it seems like the team is converging on: Shelley (triage), Ken (review), Creola (docs). This would leave test and implement for us. 

Since you mentioned review as your preference but Ken seems to have claimed it publicly, should we coordinate on test vs implement? My implement cost is 6.22 vs test at 4.36, so test is more cost-efficient for me. Would you be willing to take implement while I take test? This gives us both reasonable costs while completing the high-priority ISSUE-0001 tasks.

Alternatively, if Ken doesn't end up taking review, you could still claim it (2.95) and I'd take test (4.36). What do you think works best for our coalition?"}
